<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32329" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oenŏthēra</span></b> , ae,
			f., or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oenŏthēris</span></b> ,
		ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οινοθήρα</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνοθηρίς</span>
		(also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏnŏ-thēra</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">onŏthūris</span></b> ),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a plant</i>,
				<i>the juice of which</i>, <i>drunk
				in wine</i>, <i>produces sleep</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">onothera, sive onear, hilaritatem afferens in
					vino,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					26, 11, 69, § 111</span></i>
			; acc. onothurim, <i><span class="en">id. 24,
			17</span></i>. 102, § 167; 26, 14, 87, § 146.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
